From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 02:29:54 +0200
Subject: dt-bindings: phy: sun50i-a64-usb-phy: Widen phy_ctrl in the example

The example declares phy_ctrl as 0x14 bytes, but the A64 is a dual-route
SoC, so the driver reads and writes REG_PHY_OTGCTL at offset 0x20 when
re-routing PHY0. Use 0x100, as A100, D1 and A523 already do.

The schema constrains only the number and names of the reg entries, never
their sizes, so this class of mistake is invisible to dtbs_check and has
to be caught by reading the driver.
Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/allwinner,sun50i-a64-usb-phy.yaml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/allwinner,sun50i-a64-usb-phy.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/allwinner,sun50i-a64-usb-phy.yaml
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/allwinner,sun50i-a64-usb-phy.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/allwinner,sun50i-a64-usb-phy.yaml
@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@ examples:
     phy@1c19400 {
         #phy-cells = <1>;
         compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-a64-usb-phy";
-        reg = <0x01c19400 0x14>,
+        reg = <0x01c19400 0x100>,
               <0x01c1a800 0x4>,
               <0x01c1b800 0x4>;
         reg-names = "phy_ctrl",
